{#-
Extractors:
  - places: AnchorExtractor("<PLACES>", "</PLACES>")
-#}
<|SECTION:TASK|>
New place names came up in the scene. Put each one into the world's map of places.

Known places:
{% for place in known_places -%}
- {{ place }}
{% else -%}
- none yet
{% endfor %}
Cultures and where they live:
{% for culture in cultures -%}
- {{ culture.name }}{% if culture.places %}: {{ culture.places|join(', ') }}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if current_place -%}
The scene is in: {{ current_place }}
{% endif -%}
{% if recent_text %}
The last lines of the scene:
{{ recent_text }}
{% endif %}
New place names: {{ names|join(', ') }}

Write exactly one line per name, in this format:
Name | kind | parent | cultures | sure or unsure

- kind: one of {{ kinds|join(', ') }}.
- parent: the known place or new place it lies in, spelled as given, or none.
- cultures: inherit if its people are like its parent's, else culture names with shares adding up to 100, like "{{ example_shares }}".
- sure or unsure: unsure when the scene doesn't make it clear.

If a name is not a place (a person, or a thing such as a stall or a ship), write this line for it instead:
Name | skip

Example line:
Oakford | village | {{ example_parent }} | inherit | sure

Answer only with the lines, inside <PLACES></PLACES>.
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{{ set_prepared_response("<PLACES>\n") }}
